00:29:37.345 --> 00:29:38.945
because they're fast and furious.

00:29:38.945 --> 00:29:41.385
But they're always directed
towards the larger purpose

00:29:41.385 --> 00:29:42.735
of what we're trying to do.

00:29:43.925 --> 00:29:46.545
- Yeah, no, I have to, you
spent more time with them,

00:29:46.545 --> 00:29:49.495
but in my interactions, Bill is one

00:29:49.495 --> 00:29:51.795
of the few people that in my meeting

00:29:51.795 --> 00:29:54.455
he he's able to push
out and he pushes hard

00:29:54.455 --> 00:29:55.565
on all the exact right places.

00:29:55.565 --> 00:29:56.985
How do we know we're
reaching the right kids?

00:29:56.985 --> 00:29:58.055
How do we know we're getting traction?

00:29:58.055 --> 00:29:59.155
How do we know we're supporting teachers?

00:29:59.155 --> 00:30:00.605
How do we know?

00:30:00.605 --> 00:30:03.085
And then like the next meeting
could be with people who are

00:30:03.085 --> 00:30:04.875
like working on healthcare

00:30:04.875 --> 00:30:07.107
or fighting polio or whatever.

00:30:07.107 --> 00:30:09.335
And then he pushes them too

00:30:09.335 --> 00:30:11.235
like these are the experts in the field.

00:30:11.235 --> 00:30:13.625
So I don't feel as bad.

00:30:13.625 --> 00:30:15.115
And not being intimidated by Bill

00:30:15.115 --> 00:30:17.365
is easier said than
done, but it's good until

00:30:20.245 --> 00:30:21.648
It's easier said than done.

00:30:22.635 --> 00:30:24.405
Let's see, in the, I see we're almost

00:30:24.405 --> 00:30:29.405
out of time but let's make sure
I have a one more question.

00:30:30.195 --> 00:30:32.735
Well, this is a question
from Charles Lamar Dreyden

00:30:32.735 --> 00:30:36.444
on Facebook asking, is there, well, I'll

00:30:36.444 --> 00:30:38.448
I'll paraphrase the question,

00:30:39.328 --> 00:30:41.028
your use on standardized testing.

00:30:41.028 --> 00:30:41.985
And the question is
saying measurement tools

00:30:41.985 --> 00:30:44.725
showing correlation between
success in standardized testing

00:30:44.725 --> 00:30:46.495
but what are your views
on standardized testing?

00:30:46.495 --> 00:30:48.115
It's a bit of a hot
topic, but I always say

00:30:48.115 --> 00:30:48.948
what part do you disagree,

00:30:48.948 --> 00:30:50.335
with the standardized or the testing?

00:30:50.335 --> 00:30:52.305
Or is there something
else or how you use it?

00:30:52.305 --> 00:30:54.415
How do you do it

00:30:54.415 --> 00:30:55.565
- I think tests are important.

00:30:55.565 --> 00:30:58.365
I think we need to be innovating
a lot more in this space

00:30:58.365 --> 00:30:59.875
to be honest with you.

00:30:59.875 --> 00:31:02.915
one thing that's fascinating
is grades are very predictive

00:31:02.915 --> 00:31:05.445
of adult success,
extraordinarily predictive.

00:31:05.445 --> 00:31:06.975
That may be a matter of statistics.

00:31:06.975 --> 00:31:10.565
It's multiple opportunities
to view some young person.

00:31:10.565 --> 00:31:14.485
It has SEL and executive
function skills embedded in it.

00:31:14.485 --> 00:31:16.515
It can also be very damaging to a student

00:31:16.515 --> 00:31:19.905
if it doesn't really include
opportunities to rethink

00:31:19.905 --> 00:31:21.315
and redo work.

00:31:21.315 --> 00:31:24.775
So I think we need assessments
I think testing is good.

00:31:24.775 --> 00:31:28.165
I think part of learning
is having a little anxiety

00:31:28.165 --> 00:31:30.075
with what you're learning to retain it

00:31:30.075 --> 00:31:32.055
and then ultimately synthesizing it

00:31:32.055 --> 00:31:33.665
with other things over
the course of the year.

00:31:33.665 --> 00:31:36.575
But we need to make sure
that the tests we give are

00:31:36.575 --> 00:31:39.215
are usable for families
usable for students and

00:31:39.215 --> 00:31:43.615
and ultimately usable to advance equity.

00:31:43.615 --> 00:31:46.319
So I think the, I guess the,

00:31:46.319 --> 00:31:50.185
the reality for me is there
four things we ask tests to do

00:31:50.185 --> 00:31:51.115
and it may be too many.

00:31:51.115 --> 00:31:52.445
We need to start thinking about that.

00:31:52.445 --> 00:31:55.905
We need tests to give students
feedback on where they are.

00:31:55.905 --> 00:31:58.535
We need tests to give teachers feedback

00:31:58.535 --> 00:32:01.005
on where students are and
what they should do next.

00:32:01.005 --> 00:32:04.145
We need tests that enable
us to compare schools

00:32:04.145 --> 00:32:05.225
and make sure we're living

00:32:05.225 --> 00:32:07.475
up to our equity responsibilities.

00:32:07.475 --> 00:32:10.445
And ultimately we need
tests to place students

00:32:10.445 --> 00:32:13.315
at the next level of education
in ways that are appropriate

00:32:13.315 --> 00:32:16.025
with their skills,
interests, and abilities.

00:32:16.025 --> 00:32:20.575
So, I think need to do a
lot more in assessment.

00:32:20.575 --> 00:32:22.325
And I think that the
foundation we're committed

00:32:22.325 --> 00:32:23.618
to innovating around it.

00:32:25.045 --> 00:32:26.985
- No, I couldn't couldn't agree more. T

00:32:26.985 --> 00:32:27.818
here's nothing wrong with testing

00:32:27.818 --> 00:32:29.675
nothing wrong with standardized.

00:32:29.675 --> 00:32:30.508
But there's other ways to do it,

00:32:30.508 --> 00:32:33.295
because now when you do
work on an online platform,

00:32:33.295 --> 00:32:36.385
it is standardized and it
is assessing where you are.

00:32:36.385 --> 00:32:39.055
But as continuous, it can be
part of part of the learning.

00:32:39.055 --> 00:32:40.855
And also you can make it more actionable.

